{{#> modal overlayId="credits-overlay" modalId="credits-modal" title="Credits"}}
    <p>
        All visual and game design for <i>Pixel Juggle</i> is the original work of <a href="https://elana.games" target="_blank">Elana Bell Bogdan</a>. The underlying code was written in Cursor, using the Sonnet 5 and Composer 2.5 models.
    </p>

    <h3>Third-party code</h3>
    <ul class="credits-list">
        <li>
            <strong><a href="https://github.com/PavelDoGreat/WebGL-Fluid-Simulation" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WebGL Fluid Simulation</a></strong>
            by Pavel DoGreat (<a href="https://github.com/PavelDoGreat/WebGL-Fluid-Simulation/blob/master/LICENSE" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">MIT License</a>). The background fluid effect adapts this project&rsquo;s WebGL approach &mdash; which, in turn, implements Jos Stam&rsquo;s &ldquo;Stable Fluids&rdquo; technique.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Siteswap notation</h3>
    <p>
        Pattern parsing and validation were written for this project, following standard siteswap conventions. In particular, vanilla patterns use the average and permutation tests, while synchronous patterns use beat-pair notation with crossing 'x' suffixes, and the slide property for validity.
    </p>
    <p class="credits-references-label">References consulted:</p>
    <ul class="credits-list">
        <li>
